id: pm-vcs-wm40
title: "Phase 3: distribution over a real transport"
description: "Bundles let two repositories exchange history offline, which is enough to prove the object model but is not distribution. This phase adds named remotes, remote-tracking refs, and clone, fetch and push over a transport, with object negotiation computed from reachability rather than sending the whole store, and non-fast-forward pushes refused by default."
type: Epic
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:24.061Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T02:39:02.846Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-02T21:36:35.486Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-02T21:36:35.486Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "pm vcs clone produces a repository whose object closure is identical to the source, whose branches arrive under refs/remotes/origin, and which checks out the branch the source's HEAD names; fetch transfers only objects the receiver lacks; push refuses a non-fast-forward without an explicit override and never leaves a ref pointing at an object that was not transferred; remote-tracking refs live under refs/remotes and are never confused with local branches; a push may only move branches and tags; the remote ref advances only through a compare-and-swap against the value the pusher observed, so a lost race fails the push rather than clobbering the winner; bundles and fully local repositories remain usable without a configured or reachable remote"
