notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T19:32:31.852Z",codex,"Epic Lore research adds stable repository and branch identities,resumable missing-object transfer,server-side closure verification,capability negotiation,and a final compare-and-swap ref publication while retaining bundles and offline repositories."
  "2026-08-03T02:39:02.846Z","harness:claude-code","Two criteria were removed here and now live on pm-vcs-i4au, for the phase that has a wire: resumable missing-object upload, and peer capability and repository format negotiation. Both were added from the Lore research note on 2026-08-01 and describe a network protocol; the filesystem transport has no interruption to resume from and no peer to disagree with. Deferral rationale is decision pm-vcs-6qva. The clone criterion previously said the clone's refs are identical to the source's, which contradicts the clone contract in pm-vcs-jj9r: source branches arrive under refs/remotes/origin and only the branch HEAD names is created locally."
close_reason: "Phase 3 complete: remotes, transport interface, fetch/push/clone shipped with reachability-based negotiation, receiver-side fast-forward refusal and compare-and-swap ref updates."
body: ""
